Ladybird’s seccomp policy allows the TCGETS and TIOCGWINSZ ioctls,
which glibc’s and musl’s isatty() use. Gecko’s SandboxFilter.cpp
names the same split between the two libcs, but answers both requests
with ENOTTY, so isatty() is always false there. Chromium’s
RestrictIoctl() allows TCGETS and FIONREAD and kills the process for
anything else, TIOCGWINSZ included; Chromium doesn’t support musl.
Ladybird already allows TCGETS, and logs in color to a terminal, so
allowing TIOCGWINSZ too keeps that the same under musl. From reading
the sources.
